{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794860896418,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_7243a9ea90614559910909c9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_parcels.py"},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_parcels.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import unittest\n2: from datetime import date, datetime\n3: from decimal import Decimal\n4: \n5: from parcels.delivery import add_working_days, delivery_date\n6: from parcels.packing import parcel_weights\n7: from parcels.quote import CannotShip, shipping_cost\n8: \n9: \n10: class ParcelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n11:     def test_heavy_orders_are_split_evenly(self):\n12:         self.assertEqual(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\")), [Decimal(\"23.334\")] * 3)\n13: \n14:     def test_free_shipping_and_destinations(self):\n15:         self.assertEqual(shipping_cost(Decimal(\"80\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"de\"), Decimal(\"0.00\"))\n16:         with self.assertRaises(CannotShip):\n17:             shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"1\"), \"US\")\n18: \n19:     def test_weekends_are_skipped(self):\n20:         self.assertEqual(add_working_days(date(2026, 3, 6), 1), date(2026, 3, 9))\n21:         self.assertEqual(delivery_date(datetime(2026, 3, 5, 16, 0), \"NL\"), date(2026, 3, 10))\n22: \n23: \n24: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n25:     unittest.main()\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import unittest\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom parcels.delivery import add_working_days, delivery_date\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import CannotShip, shipping_cost\n\n\nclass ParcelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_heavy_orders_are_split_evenly(self):\n        self.assertEqual(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\")), [Decimal(\"23.334\")] * 3)\n\n    def test_free_shipping_and_destinations(self):\n        self.assertEqual(shipping_cost(Decimal(\"80\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"de\"), Decimal(\"0.00\"))\n        with self.assertRaises(CannotShip):\n            shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"1\"), \"US\")\n\n    def test_weekends_are_skipped(self):\n        self.assertEqual(add_working_days(date(2026, 3, 6), 1), date(2026, 3, 9))","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_parcels.py","text":"import unittest\nfrom datetime import date, datetime\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom parcels.delivery import add_working_days, delivery_date\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import CannotShip, shipping_cost\n\n\nclass ParcelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_heavy_orders_are_split_evenly(self):\n        self.assertEqual(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\")), [Decimal(\"23.334\")] * 3)\n\n    def test_free_shipping_and_destinations(self):\n        self.assertEqual(shipping_cost(Decimal(\"80\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"de\"), Decimal(\"0.00\"))\n        with self.assertRaises(CannotShip):\n            shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"1\"), \"US\")\n\n    def test_weekends_are_skipped(self):\n        self.assertEqual(add_working_days(date(2026, 3, 6), 1), date(2026, 3, 9))\n        self.assertEqual(delivery_date(datetime(2026, 3, 5, 16, 0), \"NL\"), date(2026, 3, 10))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/test_parcels.py","time":{"start":1794860896386,"end":1794860896411}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me read the tests too, to check behavior expectations.\n\nAlso I need to verify the Friday 17:00 delivery date calculation. Let me check the add_working_days logic.\n\nQ1: FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_FREE_FROM\", \"60.00\")) — free from €60. Changed via env var PARCELS_FREE_FROM.\n\nQ2: Heavy order split into multiple parcels via parcel_weights. What happens to an order heavier than a single parcel may be? It gets split into as many parcels as needed, each at most MAX_PARCEL_KG = 31.5 kg, all of the same weight (rounded up to gram). Shipping cost is summed per parcel. Note the rounding up to the gram means the sum of parcel weights may exceed total weight. Also there's no upper limit on total weight — MAX_PARCEL_KG is per parcel.\n\nNote: parcel_price uses math.ceil(weight_kg) for per_kg — price per started kg. So each parcel's price is base + per_kg * ceil(kg).\n\nQ3: Default carrier is \"postnl\" (settings.py:10), changed via env var PARCELS_CARRIER, must be one of \"dhl\", \"ups\", \"postnl\" else RuntimeError at import.\n\nQ4: Friday at 17:00. CUTOFF_HOUR = 15, so hour >= 15 → start += 1 day → Saturday. add_working_days(Saturday, HANDLING_DAYS + transit). For country NL: transit=1, handling=1 → 2 working days from Saturday → Saturday+1 = Sunday (skipped, not counted), Monday counts (days=1), Tuesday counts (days=0) → Tuesday. So NL: Tuesday. For DE: transit 2, handling 1 → 3 working days → Monday(1), Tuesday(2), Wednesday(3) → Wednesday. For other countries (default 4) → 5 working days → Thursday.\n\nWait: careful — add_working_days(start=Saturday, days=2): current=Sat; loop: current += 1 → Sun, weekday=6, not <5, days stays 2. current += 1 → Mon, weekday 0 <5 → days=1. current += 1 → Tue → days=0 → return Tuesday. Yes, Tuesday.\n\nFor DE (3 working days): Sun(skip), Mon(2), Tue(1), Wed(0) → Wednesday.\n\nDefault transit 4 → 5 working days → Thu.\n\nHmm, but note the day-of-week: Friday at 17:00 → start = Saturday (Saturday). Wait: start = ordered.date() = Friday; ordered.hour = 17 >= 15 → start += 1 day = Saturday. Then add_working_days from Saturday skips Sat and Sun. So handling effectively begins Monday.\n\nHmm, but the deadline of question: \"delivery date for an order placed on a Friday at 17:00\" — depends on country. Let me compute exact dates for a concrete date. E.g. Friday 2026-01-09 at 17:00 → start Saturday 2026-01-10. NL → Tuesday 2026-01-13. DE → Wednesday 2026-01-14. Others → Thursday 2026-01-15.\n\nLet me verify with Python.\n\nAlso note: holidays are NOT accounted for — docstring says \"holidays are not\" skipped (delivery.py:15). Only weekends are skipped.\n\nLet me read the tests to confirm expectations.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e60bcd150013XNa8fCcc8H60A","sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","messageID":"msg_1e60bb60a001OdHTY628jdw68H"}}
