{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794860911927,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_79d394ea63064c0a85b12b69","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, date\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date, add_working_days\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\n# Friday at 17:00\nfor d in [\"2026-03-06\", \"2026-01-09\", \"2026-07-03\"]:\n    fri = datetime.fromisoformat(d + \"T17:00\")\n    print(d, \"weekday:\", fri.strftime(\"%A\"))\n    for c in [\"NL\", \"DE\", \"BE\", \"LU\", \"FR\", \"GB\"]:\n        try:\n            print(\"   \", c, delivery_date(fri, c), delivery_date(fri, c).strftime(\"%A\"))\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(\"   \", c, \"err\", e)\nPY"},"output":"2026-03-06 weekday: Friday\n    NL 2026-03-10 Tuesday\n    DE 2026-03-11 Wednesday\n    BE 2026-03-11 Wednesday\n    LU 2026-03-11 Wednesday\n    FR 2026-03-13 Friday\n    GB 2026-03-13 Friday\n2026-01-09 weekday: Friday\n    NL 2026-01-13 Tuesday\n    DE 2026-01-14 Wednesday\n    BE 2026-01-14 Wednesday\n    LU 2026-01-14 Wednesday\n    FR 2026-01-16 Friday\n    GB 2026-01-16 Friday\n2026-07-03 weekday: Friday\n    NL 2026-07-07 Tuesday\n    DE 2026-07-08 Wednesday\n    BE 2026-07-08 Wednesday\n    LU 2026-07-08 Wednesday\n    FR 2026-07-10 Friday\n    GB 2026-07-10 Friday\n","metadata":{"output":"2026-03-06 weekday: Friday\n    NL 2026-03-10 Tuesday\n    DE 2026-03-11 Wednesday\n    BE 2026-03-11 Wednesday\n    LU 2026-03-11 Wednesday\n    FR 2026-03-13 Friday\n    GB 2026-03-13 Friday\n2026-01-09 weekday: Friday\n    NL 2026-01-13 Tuesday\n    DE 2026-01-14 Wednesday\n    BE 2026-01-14 Wednesday\n    LU 2026-01-14 Wednesday\n    FR 2026-01-16 Friday\n    GB 2026-01-16 Friday\n2026-07-03 weekday: Friday\n    NL 2026-07-07 Tuesday\n    DE 2026-07-08 Wednesday\n    BE 2026-07-08 Wednesday\n    LU 2026-07-08 Wednesday\n    FR 2026-07-10 Friday\n    GB 2026-07-10 Friday\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, date\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date, add_working_days\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\n# Friday at 17:00\nfor d in [\"2026-03-06\", \"2026-01-09\", \"2026-07-03\"]:\n    fri = datetime.fromisoformat(d + \"T17:00\")\n    print(d, \"weekday:\", fri.strftime(\"%A\"))\n    for c in [\"NL\", \"DE\", \"BE\", \"LU\", \"FR\", \"GB\"]:\n        try:\n            print(\"   \", c, delivery_date(fri, c), delivery_date(fri, c).strftime(\"%A\"))\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(\"   \", c, \"err\", e)\nPY","time":{"start":1794860911556,"end":1794860911899}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me verify the Friday 17:00 delivery date calculation by running the code.\n\nFriday 17:00 — CUTOFF_HOUR = 15, so 17 >= 15 → start = Saturday. Then add_working_days(start=Saturday, HANDLING_DAYS + transit).\n\nFor NL: transit=1, HANDLING=1 → 2 working days from Saturday: Sat → +1 = Sunday (skipped), Monday (count 1), Tuesday (count 2) → Tuesday.\n\nWait let's trace add_working_days(start=Saturday, days=2):\ncurrent = Saturday; loop: current += 1 day → Sunday, weekday 6, not < 5, days stays 2. current += 1 → Monday, weekday 0 <5, days=1. current += 1 → Tuesday, days=0 → return Tuesday.\n\nSo NL Friday 17:00 → Tuesday.\n\nTest asserts delivery_date(datetime(2026, 3, 5, 16, 0), \"NL\") == date(2026, 3, 10). 2026-03-05 is a Thursday. 16:00 >= 15 → start = Friday 2026-03-06. add_working_days(Fri, 2) → Sat(skip), Sun(skip), Mon(1), Tue(2) → 2026-03-10. ✓\n\nFor DE: transit=2, +1 handling = 3 working days from Saturday → Sunday skip, Monday 1, Tuesday 2, Wednesday 3 → Wednesday.\nFor other countries (default 4) + 1 = 5 working days from Saturday → Mon 1, Tue 2, Wed 3, Thu 4, Fri 5 → next Friday.\n\nLet me verify with a quick run.\n\nAlso note: holidays are NOT accounted for (docstring says \"holidays are not\").\n\nQ2: heavy order — split into multiple parcels. parcel_weights: count = ceil(total/31.5), each = ceil to gram. Note the rounding up to the gram means total weight may slightly exceed. Also note: shipping cost is per-parcel summed. Also note: with the \"each\" weight rounded up to gram, per_kg price is charged per started kg per parcel (math.ceil(weight_kg)) — so per parcel price = base + per_kg * ceil(kg).\n\nAlso note the potential subtlety: if total_kg > 0 but tiny... `count = max(1, ceil(...))`. And the total rounded-up weights could exceed MAX_PARCEL_KG? Let's check: count = ceil(total/31.5). each = ceil_to_gram(total/count). Each is at most total/count + 0.001 which for count>=2 is ≤ total/2 + 0.001 ≤ 31.5 + 0.001 potentially? For count=1, total ≤ 31.5, each = ceil_to_gram(total) which could be 31.5 exactly or slightly more (e.g. total = 31.5004 → count = 2). For count = 1, total ≤ 31.5 so each ≤ 31.5 (rounded up to gram could be 31.5 max). Actually total=31.5 → each=31.5 exactly. Fine. Edge: total = 31.5000001 → count = 2.\n\nHmm, but a subtle bug: count=1 requires total ≤ 31.5, each = ceil_gram(total) ≤ 31.5 since 31.5 is a whole gram. Good.\n\nAlso the per-parcel charge uses math.ceil(weight_kg) — weight in whole kg started.\n\nQ1: Free shipping from €60.00 (FREE_SHIPPING_FROM). \"Orders at or above this value (in euros, after discounts) ship for free inside the EU.\" Changed without editing code: set env var PARCELS_FREE_FROM. Note shipping_cost checks `order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM` → Decimal comparison with strings. Also note: free shipping threshold applies inside EU only (the country check happens first; non-EU raises CannotShip anyway).\n\nAlso note: FREE_SHIPPING_FROM env var value isn't validated — a bad value would raise InvalidOperation at import time.\n\nQ3: default carrier is \"postnl\" (settings.py:10), env var PARCELS_CARRIER. Must be one of CARRIERS = (\"dhl\", \"ups\", \"postnl\"), else RuntimeError at import. Read once at import time — so changing the env var requires restart.\n\nAlso note the carrier affects TARIFFS lookup and the free shipping threshold is not carrier-specific.\n\nLet me run a few commands to verify behavior.\n\nAlso check: does the carrier choice affect delivery times? No — delivery uses TRANSIT_DAYS by country, not carrier.\n\nLet me verify the Friday 17:00 dates with actual execution, and check holidays handling.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e60c0884001hqoKJnb3Oii3M1","sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","messageID":"msg_1e60be3d6001mD7OIdhnRNJiNU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794860912686,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_8ee8f2490ea84ccb8ff143d9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost\nfrom parcels.settings import FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, CARRIER, MAX_PARCEL_KG\nprint(\"FREE_SHIPPING_FROM:\", FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, \"CARRIER:\", CARRIER, \"MAX:\", MAX_PARCEL_KG)\nfor w in [\"1\", \"31.5\", \"32\", \"40\", \"70\", \"100\", \"0.001\"]:\n    print(w, parcel_weights(Decimal(w)))\nprint(\"cost 32kg DE:\", shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"32\"), \"DE\"))\nprint(\"cost 32kg NL:\", shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"32\"), \"NL\"))\nprint(\"cost 59.99 NL:\", shipping_cost(Decimal(\"59.99\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"NL\"))\nprint(\"cost 60.00 NL:\", shipping_cost(Decimal(\"60.00\"), Decimal(\"2\"), \"NL\"))\nPY"},"output":"FREE_SHIPPING_FROM: 60.00 CARRIER: postnl MAX: 31.5\n1 [Decimal('1.000')]\n31.5 [Decimal('31.500')]\n32 [Decimal('16.000'), Decimal('16.000')]\n40 [Decimal('20.000'), Decimal('20.000')]\n70 [Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334')]\n100 [Decimal('25.000'), Decimal('25.000'), Decimal('25.000'), Decimal('25.000')]\n0.001 [Decimal('0.001')]\ncost 32kg DE: 37.10\ncost 32kg NL: 22.60\ncost 59.99 NL: 5.00\ncost 60.00 NL: 0.00\n","metadata":{"output":"FREE_SHIPPING_FROM: 60.00 CARRIER: postnl MAX: 31.5\n1 [Decimal('1.000')]\n31.5 [Decimal('31.500')]\n32 [Decimal('16.000'), Decimal('16.000')]\n40 [Decimal('20.000'), Decimal('20.000')]\n70 [Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334'), Decimal('23.334')]\n100 [Decimal('25.000'), Decimal('25.000'), Decimal('25.000'), Decimal('25.000')]\n0.001 [Decimal('0.001')]\ncost 32kg DE: 37.10\ncost 32kg NL: 22.60\ncost 59.99 NL: 5.00\ncost 60.00 NL: 0.00\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.packi