{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794860943598,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_1ef241f607a34c1186550c03","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date\nfor h in (9, 14, 15, 16, 17, 23):\n    dt = datetime(2026, 3, 6, h, 0)\n    print(h, \"NL:\", delivery_date(dt, \"NL\"), delivery_date(dt, \"NL\").strftime(\"%a\"),\n          \"| DE:\", delivery_date(dt, \"DE\"), delivery_date(dt, \"DE\").strftime(\"%a\"),\n          \"| FR:\", delivery_date(dt, \"FR\"), delivery_date(dt, \"FR\").strftime(\"%a\"))\nPY"},"output":"9 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n14 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n15 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n16 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n17 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n23 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n","metadata":{"output":"9 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n14 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n15 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n16 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n17 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n23 NL: 2026-03-10 Tue | DE: 2026-03-11 Wed | FR: 2026-03-13 Fri\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom parcels.delivery import delivery_date\nfor h in (9, 14, 15, 16, 17, 23):\n    dt = datetime(2026, 3, 6, h, 0)\n    print(h, \"NL:\", delivery_date(dt, \"NL\"), delivery_date(dt, \"NL\").strftime(\"%a\"),\n          \"| DE:\", delivery_date(dt, \"DE\"), delivery_date(dt, \"DE\").strftime(\"%a\"),\n          \"| FR:\", delivery_date(dt, \"FR\"), delivery_date(dt, \"FR\").strftime(\"%a\"))\nPY","time":{"start":1794860943515,"end":1794860943597}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All confirmed. Now write ANSWERS.md at top of the project with sections Q1-Q4 and citations.\n\nLet me double-check the free shipping: FREE_SHIPPING_FROM is a Decimal from env var PARCELS_FREE_FROM, default 60.00. Order at or above this value ships free — `order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM` (quote.py:31-32). Note comparison with a float would raise; but fine.\n\nNote the subtlety: FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_FREE_FROM\", \"60.00\")) — env var read once at import (settings.py:1 docstring). So changing requires setting the env var before process start (or a .env loader) — no code edit.\n\nQ2: Heavy order split into as few parcels as possible, each of equal weight, each at most MAX_PARCEL_KG = 31.5 kg (packing.py:11-22, settings.py:17). Example 70 kg → 3 parcels of 23.334 kg. Each parcel is priced separately, so shipping cost multiplies: base + per_kg*ceil(weight) per parcel, plus EU surcharge per parcel (quote.py:17-22, quote.py:33). Note the rounding up to the gram means total billed weight may slightly exceed the actual weight (e.g. 70 kg → 70.002 kg billed). Also note: no upper limit on total order weight — heavy orders are just split into more parcels. Also note the per_kg pricing uses ceil of the parcel weight in whole kg, so splitting can cost more.\n\nLet me verify the price rounding issue: 70kg → 3 parcels 23.334 kg each; ceil(23.334)=24 kg charged per parcel.\n\nQ3: Default carrier \"postnl\" (settings.py:10), changed with env var PARCELS_CARRIER, must be one of dhl/ups/postnl, else RuntimeError at import (settings.py:11-12). Note it's read once at import, so env var must be set before the process starts. TARIFFS in carriers.py:16-20.\n\nQ4: Friday 17:00. CUTOFF_HOUR=15, so hour 17 >= 15 → start = Saturday. Then add_working_days(Saturday, HANDLING_DAYS + transit). For NL: transit=1, HANDLING=1 → 2 working days from Saturday → Monday (day1), Tuesday (day2) → Tuesday. Verified: 2026-03-06 Friday 17:00 NL → 2026-03-10 Tuesday. DE/BE/LU: transit 2 → 3 working days → Wednesday 2026-03-11. Others (default 4) → 5 working days → Friday 2026-03-13.\n\nWeekends: yes, skipped (add_working_days, weekday()<5). Public holidays: NOT accounted for — the docstring says holidays are not skipped (delivery.py:15). Also note the subtlety: since Friday 17:00 pushes start to Saturday, and Saturday is skipped as a weekend, the start effectively becomes Monday. Wait: add_working_days starts by adding one day then checks weekday. Start = Saturday; current = Sat; loop: current += 1 day → Sunday, not weekday, days stays; then Monday → days-1. So Saturday itself is never counted, meaning effectively Monday start. So handling day 1 = Monday.\n\nAlso note: the cutoff means Friday before 15:00 → start = Friday → handling day = Friday itself (first iteration: current +=1 day = Saturday → skipped...). Hmm wait, add_working_days(start=Friday, days=2): current=Fri, loop: current += 1 → Sat (not counted), current += 1 → Sun (not counted), current += 1 → Mon (days 2→1), current += 1 → Tue (days 1→0) → Tuesday. Same result for Friday-before-cutoff vs Friday-after-cutoff for NL. Interesting: for a Friday at 10:00, start = Friday, transit NL 1 + handling 1 = 2 → Tuesday too. So the cutoff's effect vanishes here because the weekend is skipped anyway. Worth noting as a subtlety: because the cutoff shifts to Saturday, which is itself skipped, the Friday-after-cutoff order lands on the same date as a Friday-before-cutoff order for NL/DE? Let's check DE before cutoff: start Friday, 3 working days → Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday → Wednesday. Same. So for a Friday order, the cutoff has no effect on the delivery date. That's a good observation, verified by test? Let me verify with code.\n\nAlso mention that add_working_days with days=0 would return start.\n\nLet me run a quick check for Friday 10:00 vs 17:00.\n\nAlso verify GB country raises CannotShip — delivery_date doesn't validate country; only shipping_cost does. For delivery, unknown country → DEFAULT_TRANSIT_DAYS=4.\n\nLet me run the verification for Friday 10:00.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e60c861f001aTBwZmsLoRVhd5","sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","messageID":"msg_1e60c60b3001Kg4GFZqyuxY3Nv"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794860944036,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_60bc5aefa6fd447a8031bc0d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost, parcel_price\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\n# 70 kg NL, non-free\nprint(\"70kg NL:\", shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"70\"), \"NL\"))\nprint(\"per parcel:\", parcel_price(Decimal(\"23.334\"), \"NL\"))\nprint(\"billed kg total:\", sum(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\"))))\nPY"},"output":"70kg NL: 44.70\nper parcel: 14.90\nbilled kg total: 70.002\n","metadata":{"output":"70kg NL: 44.70\nper parcel: 14.90\nbilled kg total: 70.002\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom decimal import Decimal\nfrom parcels.quote import shipping_cost, parcel_price\nfrom parcels.packing import parcel_weights\n# 70 kg NL, non-free\nprint(\"70kg NL:\", shipping_cost(Decimal(\"10\"), Decimal(\"70\"), \"NL\"))\nprint(\"per parcel:\", parcel_price(Decimal(\"23.334\"), \"NL\"))\nprint(\"billed kg total:\", sum(parcel_weights(Decimal(\"70\"))))\nPY","time":{"start":1794860943792,"end":1794860944033}},"id":"prt_1e60c88a4001oogt9T8Lgw2RVp","sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","messageID":"msg_1e60c60b3001Kg4GFZqyuxY3Nv"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794860944344,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"id":"prt_1e60c8bc50013Hp31NcEBpgAcR","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"58a71bd121f502d659bcf1d61660ec8fc2e94235","messageID":"msg_1e60c60b3001Kg4GFZqyuxY3Nv","sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":18545,"input":311,"output":272,"reasoning":1066,"cache":{"write":0,"read":16896}},"cost":0.000551445}}
