{"type":"text","timestamp":1794860978835,"sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","part":{"id":"prt_1e60d0cf0001f7vSX5KFRXbP9f","messageID":"msg_1e60d062f001blDUo22FzDS63N","sessionID":"ses_e19f4fb81ffeOrjVO5vcAH6pd8","type":"text","text":"Created `ANSWERS.md` (no code changed; only the new file is added to the working tree).\n\n**Q1** — Free shipping from €60.00 (`parcels/settings.py:15`, used at `parcels/quote.py:31-32`); change it via the `PARCELS_FREE_FROM` env var, set before process start since settings are read once at import (`parcels/settings.py:1`).\n\n**Q2** — The order is split, not rejected: `count = ceil(total/31.5kg)` equal-weight parcels, each rounded up to the gram, so 70 kg → 3 × 23.334 kg (70.002 kg billed) (`parcels/packing.py:20-22`). Each parcel is priced separately and summed, and the EU surcharge applies per parcel (`parcels/quote.py:17-22`, `parcels/quote.py:33`).\n\n**Q3** — Default carrier is `postnl` (`parcels/settings.py:10`); choose another with `PARCELS_CARRIER` set to `dhl`/`ups`/`postnl`, and any other value raises `RuntimeError` at import (`parcels/settings.py:8`, `parcels/settings.py:11-12`).\n\n**Q4** — Friday 17:00 is past the 15:00 cut-off (`parcels/delivery.py:11`), so the start day is Saturday; weekends are skipped (`parcels/delivery.py:14-22`) and 1 handling day + transit days are added (`parcels/delivery.py:30`): NL → Tuesday, DE/BE/LU → Wednesday, other EU → Friday. Public holidays are **not** accounted for (`parcels/delivery.py:15` — no holiday calendar exists in the package).","time":{"start":1794860977392,"end":1794860978777}}}
